  "notes": "Modified cash basis ESU; governmental funds only (General and Depreciation funds; no enterprise funds). Receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column on trimmed pp4-5. Balance sheet from the Statement of Net Position (p1), cash basis, no liabilities. Detail uses the account-code budget-and-actual schedule (pp9-10) as the most detailed; the program-level budget schedule (pp11-12), General Fund schedule (pp13-14, identical to the total) and Depreciation Fund schedule (p15, all zero) were not repeated to avoid double counting. The account-code total receipts 8,344,422 and disbursements 7,434,686 include the sale-of-property proceeds (+1,675) and non-program (9000) 5,694 as other financing. Expenditures by account code have no object breakdown (not itemized); function categories assigned by me (SPED services and federal programs as instruction). Other financing is Miscellaneous (5,694) + sale of property 1,675. Rolls forward: 5,217,695 + 8,342,746 - 7,428,991 - 4,019 = 6,127,431. Read pages 1-15 of 15 Detail codes 2141-2161 (psychological, speech, OT; state function 2100 support services-pupils) are categorized support services, although the statement (pp4-5) includes them in 'Special education services' (1,125,688 + 2,671,963 = 1200 + 1296 + 2141-2161 lines)."
